TY  - JOUR
AU  - Munoz, Jaime J. Lacueva
AU  - Fernandez, Jose Saldana
TI  - ELECTORS AND PARLIAMENTARIANS BETWEEN TWO SHORES: RELATIONS AND POLITICAL REPRESENTATION AMONG THE CHILEAN COMMUNITY RESIDING IN SPAIN, 1810-1820
T2  - TEMAS AMERICANISTAS
M3  - Article
AB  - Based on an analysis of the electoral documentation of the convocation of the Cortes in 1810 and 1820, and employing a prosopographical approach, this article focuses on the Chilean community residing in Spain during a period of profound institutional uncertainty. In this context, beyond political activity, permeated the daily lives of individuals and conditioned their life trajectories. From the perspective of migration, this study examines the characteristics that defined the electoral body and how these were projected onto political identities and positions that were still in progress, ranging from alignment with the interests of the capital's elite to an increasing disconnection from the groups they represented. The aim is to identify lines of continuity and difference between the profiles of the individuals who exercised political representation of Chile in the Peninsula in both electoral processes. Furthermore, this study aims to open up possibilities for a deeper analysis of the political space during a period defined by the crisis of the hispanic monarchy, the unraveling of colonial relationships, and the configuration of the emerging Latin American state realities.
