TY  - JOUR
AU  - Koch, Tomas
AU  - Puppato, Lucian
AU  - Labrana, Julio
TI  - How to Align Science and Politics in the Context of Competitive Funding: An Analysis of Political Interest in Science and Public Fund Allocation in Chile (1982-2021)
T2  - LATIN AMERICAN POLICY
M3  - Article
AB  - This article examines the relationship between the principles of scientific excellence and equity in national science policy in Chile, a semi-peripheral country. It seeks to understand how political priorities influence the distribution of scientific resources and how these influences interact with disciplinary and institutional contexts. The study analyzes data on the allocation of publicly funded scientific projects in Chile 1982-2021. This quantitative dataset is complemented by a qualitative review of presidential speeches and institutional policy documents from the same period, enabling a contextual interpretation of the findings. The findings indicate that political priorities are reflected in project allocations, particularly through the promotion of certain research topics and increasing attention to gender and territorial equity. Yet, the influence of political agendas is mediated by contextual variables such as disciplinary area, the trajectories of scientific communities, and the structure of the research ecosystem. The analysis reveals a dynamic of "negotiated autonomy," in which political influence on science is present but shaped by institutional and disciplinary factors. These dynamics highlight the complex interplay between equity, excellence, and governance in the design and implementation of science policy in Chile.(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic) ((sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)) (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)1982(sic)(sic)2021(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic),(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)"(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)"(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic), (sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic),(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic)(sic).Este art & iacute;culo examina la relaci & oacute;n entre los principios de excelencia cient & iacute;fica y equidad en la pol & iacute;tica cient & iacute;fica nacional de Chile, un pa & iacute;s semiperif & eacute;rico. Busca comprender c & oacute;mo las prioridades pol & iacute;ticas influyen en la distribuci & oacute;n de los recursos cient & iacute;ficos y c & oacute;mo estas influencias interact & uacute;an con los contextos disciplinarios e institucionales. El estudio analiza datos sobre la asignaci & oacute;n de proyectos cient & iacute;ficos financiados con fondos p & uacute;blicos en Chile entre 1982 y 2021. Este conjunto de datos cuantitativos se complementa con una revisi & oacute;n cualitativa de discursos presidenciales y documentos de pol & iacute;tica institucional del mismo periodo, lo que permite una interpretaci & oacute;n contextual de los hallazgos. Los resultados indican que las prioridades pol & iacute;ticas se reflejan en la asignaci & oacute;n de proyectos, particularmente a trav & eacute;s de la promoci & oacute;n de ciertos temas de investigaci & oacute;n y de una creciente atenci & oacute;n a la equidad de g & eacute;nero y territorial. No obstante, la influencia de las agendas pol & iacute;ticas se ve mediada por variables contextuales, tales como el & aacute;rea disciplinaria, las trayectorias de las comunidades cient & iacute;ficas y la estructura del ecosistema de investigaci & oacute;n. El an & aacute;lisis revela una din & aacute;mica de "autonom & iacute;a negociada," en la cual la influencia pol & iacute;tica sobre la ciencia est & aacute; presente, pero es moldeada por factores institucionales y disciplinarios. Estas din & aacute;micas ponen de relieve la compleja interacci & oacute;n entre equidad, excelencia y gobernanza en el dise & ntilde;o y la implementaci & oacute;n de la pol & iacute;tica cient & iacute;fica en Chile.
