AU  - Cabeza, Tomas Pablo Loyola
TI  - SOCIO-POLITICAL NARRATIVES ABOUT THE CHILE OF THE PRESENT: TRANSITION TO DEMOCRACY AND SOCIAL EXPLOSION: A PRELIMINARY ASSESSMENT
T2  - HISTORIA ACTUAL ONLINE
M3  - Article
AB  - The Chile of the present has been marked, by the intellectual political debate regarding whether the Chilean transition is over or whether its end is still pending, even more so, with the two constituent processes that have been promoted in recent years. However, beyond that, much of the existing literature continues to debate an extensive and unfinished Chilean transition, to which is added the controversy regarding the origins, causes and characteristics of the social outbreak of 2019. Based on the above, the following article has the general objective of identifying, characterizing and accounting for those socio-political narratives.
