TY  - JOUR
AU  - Aravena, Pedro Rosas
TI  - From political imprisonment to exile: Humanitarian release and/or punishment in the Chilean political transition
T2  - IZQUIERDAS
M3  - Article
AB  - This article contextualizes the historical process that justified the application of the banishment penalty during the Chilean political transition. The commutation of prison sentences to exile was a means of ending the political imprisonment of the Chilean military dictatorship in a context of political and legal debates during the early transition. This measure was part of a mechanism that included policies, special laws, and a discursive framework that transcended the legal nature of the situation, appealing to the fragility of the transition and the need for social peace.
