TY  - JOUR
AU  - Garland, Daniela Cuadros
TI  - Surviving a political regime change: the Communist Party and its members on the critical events of September-December 1973 in Chile
T2  - IZQUIERDAS
M3  - Article
AB  - This article examines the political crisis following the military coup of September 1973, focusing on the four-month period of regime change. The case of Communist Party shows how defeated actors can influence the configuration of authoritarian orders. Forced into clandestinity, the party transformed fear into discipline and survival into political action, compelling the new regime to adjust its repressive mechanisms. By highlighting the role of fear, party discipline, and organizational adaptation, the article contributes to the comparative study of political parties under authoritarianism and their capacity to shape institutional orders.
