TI  - Verdejo, Inocencio, and Perejil. The dispute over the roto in Chilean political cartoons (1955-1970)
T2  - IZQUIERDAS
M3  - Article
AB  - The social and political relevance of the working classes in Chilean politics in the second third of the 20th century was also reflected and guided by cartoons. This work reveals the contested imagery of one of its most emblematic representations-the roto-through three opposing media outlets in the political arena-Topaze, El Siglo, and El Mercurio-in the context of the Cold War, linking political and heritage aspects inherent to Chilean culture.
