TY  - JOUR
AU  - Castillo, Pedro Altamirano
TI  - THE CHILEAN EXILE OF RUY MAURO MARINI: INTELLECTUAL SOCIABILITY AND POLITICAL NETWORKS SINCE CONCEPCIÓN (1970)
T2  - HISTORIA-SANTIAGO
M3  - Article
AB  - The coup d'& eacute;tat that shook Brazil in 1964 unleashed several waves of exiles, whose victims went through a complex process of relocation to countries such as Mexico, Uruguay and Chile. In these relocations, political and intellectual networks played a prominent role, disaggregated in spaces such as universities. The social scientist Ruy Mauro Marini (1932-1997) was one of the intellectuals who, after initially exiling to Mexico, was forced to leave the country again, eventually settling in Chile in the spring of Using the tools of intellectual history, this article examines the first stage of Marini's Chilean exile, that is, the time he spent in Concepci & oacute;n and his subsequent relocation to Santiago. The main objective is to analyze the intellectual sociability and political networks he established in Concepci & oacute;n. To this end we consulted the local press, university magazines in which he published, we critically reviewed his "Memoria" we conducted interviews with two direct witnesses of the time. We argue that Marini's presence in Concepci & oacute;n proves that the Latin American political networks of the operated not only in the Chilean capital and that there was close collaboration between intellectuals and the local student movement.
