TI  - 'We Were insane:' Memories and Political Cultures of Chilean Economic Elites on the Government of Salvador Allende (1970-1973)
T2  - MEMORIA Y CIVILIZACION-ANUARIO DE HISTORIA
M3  - Article
AB  - This study examines the memories of the Chilean business elite regarding the Popular Unity government (1970-1973), focusing on polarization and conflict. Based on 40 interviews with leaders of the main business organizations, both direct recollections and memories transmitted during theirformative years were collected. The testimonies evoke 'dramatic' experiences that still serve to justify the 1973 coup and reinforce adherence to rightwing positions. These negative memories shape a conservative political culture, fostering ideological cohesion within this sector.
