TY  - JOUR
AU  - Faundes Penafiel, Juan Jorge
TI  - Keys to the Chilean constituent process (2019-2022), in light of the political participation of indigenous peoples
T2  - CUHSO
M3  - Article
AB  - This paper examines the Chilean constituent process as it relates to the demands for recognition made by Chile's indigenous peoples. First, we synthesize the theoretical guidelines of what we have called a democratic, pluralistic and intercultural horizon. Second, we postulate a basic condition for the effectiveness of the rights recognized to indigenous peoples. Methodologically, among other aspects, this premises are based on comparison in contrast. Third, we formulate some critical reflections or "intercultural keys" in relation to the New Constitution Project.
