TY  - JOUR
AU  - Farias, Martin
TI  - Music and politic communication in the documentary during Chile's Popular Unity
T2  - UNIVERSUM-REVISTA DE HUMANIDADES Y CIENCIAS SOCIALES
M3  - Article
AB  - In this article, I analyse the music of three documentary films produced during the Popular Unity. I argue that a series of factors produced a shift in the use of music in documentary films from specially composed avant-garde music to pre-existent recordings. I am particularly concerned with how these recordings were pivotal in producing shared identification among the audience. At first glance, the use of music seems to be limited exclusively to the Chilean New Song repertoire, but on further inspection, a more complex scenario is revealed in which a broader range of genres and style is used to channel discourses of class struggle and political identity.
