AU  - Goicovic Donoso, Igor
TI  - Instability, Conflict and political violence in Chile, 1925-1941
T2  - HISTORIA CARIBE
M3  - Article
AB  - In the early 1920s, Chile experienced institutional instability due to the oligarchic regime crisis and the political consolidation of class movements. This crisis, which extended right until the arrival to power of the Frente Popular (1938), escalated to increasing levels of violence, involving both antagonist groups and ideologically related movements. This article analyses the circumstances and actors that shaped the scenarios of political conflict in Chile and identifies the dynamics that violence acquired.
