TY  - JOUR
AU  - Sanhueza Benavente, Maria Carolina
TI  - Road Building and Enlightened Reformism: Economic and Political Foundations in 18t h Century Chile
T2  - ANUARIO DE ESTUDIOS AMERICANOS
M3  - Article
AB  - This article th proposes that the roads built in Chile in the second half of the 18 century were the result of an infrastructure policy put forward by the Bourbons. Although these con-struction projects were first envisaged by local authorities, they only materialized when they coincided with the reformist and imperial objectives of the Spanish Monarchy. These ob-jectives included, among others, establishing a more rigid control over its domains. These reforms were developed in a context of geopolitical changes and they aimed at maximizing the extraction of economic resources under the postulates of the Enlightened ideas.
