TY  - JOUR
AU  - Carlos Rungruangsakorn, L.
TI  - The conflict impact on the political-normative design in State's role: the Chilean Republic environmental role, a case of (dis)construction
T2  - IZQUIERDAS
M3  - Article
AB  - This article aims to connect the liberal conflict theory with state role construction. In this framework, the theoretical model developed by Oszlak (2011) is approached, which explains how the state role is expressed in three levels of action: micro, meso and macro.From the above, the process of political-normative design is examined whereby the state's role in a given matter is formally manifest. For a better understanding of how the state role is created, a dialectical theoretical scheme called "Cycle of the (des)construction of the role of the State" is proposed. Subsequently, this model is applied for analyze the environmental role conformation of Chilean State, with an emphasis on its environmental impact assessment system.
